@startuml figure_apparatus
' Figure 1 - UML 2.5 activity diagram: measurement apparatus for one grounding event.
'
' Notation, all standard UML 2.5:
'   filled circle       initial node
'   rounded rectangle   action
'   diamond             decision node, guards in [square brackets]
'   solid bar           fork / join node
'   bullseye            activity final node
'
' SIZING FOR PRINT (Applied Sciences, single column, ~16 cm text width).
' The diagram's aspect ratio, not its pixel count, decides how large the text
' prints. A tall narrow diagram scaled to 16 cm runs off the page; a squarer one
' keeps both the height and the type size reasonable. Three decisions follow from
' that and should not be undone without re-measuring:
'   1. The four failure modes branch from ONE decision node, side by side, rather
'      than from nested decisions. Wide and short instead of narrow and tall.
'   2. Short outcome names; the full identifiers are expanded in the caption.
'      They were the widest row and drove the whole diagram's scale.
'   3. Explanatory notes live in the caption, and swimlanes are not used -
'      activity partitions pushed the diagram well past the printable width.

'
' PLANTUML LAYOUT FIX - DO NOT DELETE THE PADDING BELOW.
' In a four-branch switch, PlantUML drops the third branch's arrow directly
' beneath the decision node and left-aligns that branch's guard text at the
' arrow's own x, so the line is drawn straight through the label. Verified
' 11.09.2026: the collision follows the POSITION, not the wording - reordering
' the cases just moves it to whichever guard lands third, and widening the
' decision node does not move it at all. The <U+00A0> run indents that one
' guard clear of the arrow. Removing it reinstates the overlap.

skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 12

start

:Load test page and walk the DOM,
piercing shadow roots;

' Multi-line #color: action before a fork breaks the PlantUML parser (v1.2026.8);
' the line break is written as \n, not a physical newline.
#E8F0F8:**Apply attribute bundle**  ""A′ <U+2286> A""\n<b>Axis A - what is sent</b>;

#FBEDED:Remove oracle anchors;

fork
  ' Multi-line #color: action before a fork breaks the PlantUML parser (v1.2026.8);
  ' the line break is written as \n, not a physical newline.
  #E9F3E4:**Serialise observation**  ""O = R(A′, f, D)""\n<b>Axis B - how it is sent</b>;
fork again
  :Count observation tokens;
fork again
  #FBEDED:Check the ARIA path;
end fork

:Query the model, receive ""css: <selector>"";

#FBEDED:Screen the locator for anchor leakage;

:Evaluate the five-condition predicate
<b>against the raw DOM</b>;

switch (Outcome?)
case ([no stable signal in bundle])
  #F2F2F2:lacked;
case ([all five conditions met])
  #F2F2F2:success;
case ([format unreachable])
  #F2F2F2:unreachable;
case ([signal present, locator failed])
  #F2F2F2:grabbed;
endswitch

:Write grounding record (JSONL);

stop

@enduml
